    },
    "long_instructions": "### Investigate\r\n\r\n1. **Add** `fav_color` as a new variable with the value of your choice. Concatenate it onto the end of `code_name` (line 5).\r\n2. **Change** the value of `pet_name` to \"Al\". Run the program.\r\n3. **Discuss** with your partner: What happened when there weren't 3 letters to grab? Did the program break?\r\n4. **Change** the `birth_month` value to `\"\"` with nothing between the quotes. Run the program.\r\n5. **Discuss** what got added to the code name this time?\r\n6. **Now change** `birth_month` to `\" \"` with one space between the quotes. Run the program.\r\n7. **Discuss** with your partner: Compare this output to Step 4's. What's different, even though both looked empty in the code?\r\n8. **Change** the value of `pet_name` to one that's exactly 3 letters long. Talk with your partner about what you expect to happen — then run it and see.",
    "validation_file": {
      "id": "1",
      "name": "test.py",
      "contents": "import contextlib\nimport io\nfrom unittest import TestCase\n\n\nclass TestInvestigateStringConcatenation(TestCase):\n    @classmethod\n    def setUpClass(cls):\n        \"\"\"Run the student's code once and capture variables + output\"\"\"\n        with open(\"main.py\") as f:\n            cls.source = f.read()\n        cls.namespace = {}\n        stdout = io.StringIO()\n        cls.run_error = None\n        try:\n            with contextlib.redirect_stdout(stdout):\n                exec(compile(cls.source, \"main.py\", \"exec\"), cls.namespace)\n        except Exception as e:\n            cls.run_error = e\n        cls.stdout_text = stdout.getvalue()\n\n    def setUp(self):\n        if self.run_error is not None:\n            self.skipTest(f\"Your program raised an error while running: {self.run_error}.\")\n\n    def test_fav_color_added(self):\n        \"\"\"Adds a fav_color variable with a value\"\"\"\n        self.assertIn(\n            \"fav_color\", self.namespace,\n            \"We didn't find a fav_color variable. Add fav_color as a new variable with the value of your choice.\"\n        )\n\n    def test_fav_color_concatenated_onto_code_name(self):\n        \"\"\"Concatenates fav_color onto the end of the original code_name (line 5)\"\"\"\n        if \"fav_color\" not in self.namespace:\n            self.skipTest(\"Add fav_color first.\")\n        pet_name = self.namespace.get(\"pet_name\", \"\")\n        birth_month = self.namespace.get(\"birth_month\", \"\")\n        fav_color = self.namespace[\"fav_color\"]\n        expected = str(pet_name) + str(birth_month) + str(fav_color)\n        self.assertTrue(\n            any(expected in line for line in self.stdout_text.splitlines()),\n            f\"Expected the original code name to end with fav_color (looking for \\\"{expected}\\\" in the output), \"\n            \"but we didn't find it. Make sure fav_color is concatenated onto the end of code_name on line 5, \"\n            \"using the values pet_name, birth_month, and fav_color currently hold.\"\n        )",
      "folderId": "0",
